<!--
    decbench campaign case O2-noinline-mydoom-mydoom-scan_textfile (NOVEL pool:
    kuna already scored best of all decompilers on this function and the output
    was still not C, so no other decompiler surfaced this fix).

    P9 emission, leaf naming.  A PTRSUB(spacebase, off) is a reference into the
    stack frame.  P6 (link_symbol_reference) binds a Symbol to the offset
    constant only when the recovered frame layout has one; here it never can.
    The function declares a 64 KiB local buffer, so MSVC emits a stack probe
    call (_alloca_probe / __chkstk) and adjusts esp by that call's non constant
    result:

        mov  eax, 0x1003c
        call __chkstk
        sub  esp, eax            ; esp is no longer a tracked constant offset
        mov  [esp+0x18], 0       ; every frame reference stays relative to the
        mov  [esp+0x14], 0x80    ; ENTRY esp, with a dynamic PTRADD on top, and
        mov  [esp+0x10], 3       ; the offsets land outside the mapped frame

    Ghidra flags the same case with "WARNING: Unable to track spacebase fully
    for stack" and emits its unnamed stack location leaf, stack0x00000008.
    kuna instead bailed out of the SPACEBASE arm to the FUNCTIONAL render and
    emitted internal p-code into the C body:

        *(void *)PTRSUB(ESP,8)[v2] = 0;
        *(void *)PTRSUB(ESP,4)[v2] = 0x80;
        *(void *)PTRSUB(ESP,-4)[v2] = 0;

    Neither PTRSUB (an internal p-code operator) nor ESP (a raw machine
    register) is declared anywhere in the function; the body is not C.

    Stage model: P9 emission, leaf naming sub-stage (printc.rs
    push_spacebase_unnamed_ir / kuna_unnamed_location_name, the C++
    PrintC::pushUnnamedLocation leaf the SPACEBASE arm was declining to use).

    No option: this is a correctness fix (emitting an undeclared p-code
    operator and a raw register is never desired), on by default, DIV-46.
    Single pass asserts the fixed output: no PTRSUB and no raw ESP survive,
    and each of the 8 unresolvable frame references (spread over 7
    statements) renders as the self describing stack location leaf
    Stack[offset], an undeclared, extern like marker exactly like Ghidra's
    stack0x00000008.
-->
